== Final ==
F1: in 70406 the digit 4 is worth 400
F2: 437 beans, cups of ten: 43 full, 7 left, cups needed 44
F3: 2 + 5 * (8 - 3) / 5 = 7; 100 - 24 / 4 * 2 = 88
F4: 48 -> 50, 52 -> 50, estimate 2500, exact 2496, the friend's 24960 / exact = 10
F5: 7/8 = 0.875 = 87.5 %; 15 % of 60 = 9; 3/4 + 1/8 = 6/8 + 1/8 = 7/8 = 0.875
F6: 0.1 + 0.2 prints 0.3 and with 17 digits 0.30000000000000004
F7: -9 + 4 = -5; -3 - (-8) = 5; distance -12 to 7 = 19; (-3) * (-4) = 12
F8: 0 - 1 with unsigned int prints 4294967295; with int prints -1
F9: 2^6 * 2^4 = 1024 = 2^10; log2(512) = 9; 10^5 = 100000; 2^10 - 10^3 = 24
F10: 9 switches: 512 patterns; 8 switches: 256
F11: 4n - 3 at n = 6: 21; at n = -2: -11; 7a + 2 - 3a at a = 1: 6 and 4a + 2: 6; 3(x + 5) at x = 2: 21 and 3x + 15: 21
F12: 6 seats per table: table 4 seat 5 -> ticket 29; ticket 20 -> table 3, seat 2
F13: 3n + 2 at n = 7: 23 (digits read as 37 give 39)
F14: 4x - 5 = 23: x = 7, check 23; 2(x + 3) = 20: x = 7, check 20; x / 5 = 6: x = 30
F15: 12t = 3000: t = 250, check 3000; 23 = table * 5 + 3: table = 4
F16: 5x + 1 = 13: 5x = 12, x = 2.4 (whole-number division gives 2 remainder 2)
F17: d = 20 + 12t: t = 0..3 -> 20 32 44 56; t = 5 -> 80; d = 104 -> t = 7
F18: 3 * 3 + 1 = 10
F19: y = 30 - 5x at x = 4: 10; y = 0 at x = 6
F20: 0 <= i < 25 holds 25 numbers; 0 <= i <= 25 holds 26; 3x + 2 < 14 -> 3x < 12 -> x < 4; -3x > 12 -> x < -4; test x = -5: 15 > 12 is 1
F21: 75 chairs, teams of 8: teams 10 (9 teams hold 72), helpers 80, idle 5, last working ticket 74 = team 9 seat 2 (check 74), first idle ticket 75
F23 (forensic): 50 / 8 = 6 (rounded down), 6 * 8 = 48, undone 2; rounded up 7 teams, 56 helpers, idle 6
F24: cost = 3k + 2: k = 0..3 -> 2 5 8 11
